{"path":"docs/concepts/workloads/pods/scheduling-group/index.html","title":"Scheduling Group","description":"You can link a Pod to a PodGroup to indicate that the Pod belongs to a group of Pods scheduled together. This enables the scheduler to apply group-level policies such as gang scheduling rather than…","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scheduling Group"}]},{"type":"text","value":"FEATURE STATE: "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Kubernetes v1.35 [alpha]"},{"type":"text","value":"(disabled by default)"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can link a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Pod"},{"type":"text","value":" to a "},{"type":"link","href":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/podgroup-api/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"PodGroup"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to indicate that the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Pod"},{"type":"text","value":" belongs to a group of "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Pods"},{"type":"text","value":" scheduled together. This enables the scheduler to apply group-level policies such as gang scheduling rather than treating each "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Pod"},{"type":"text","value":" independently."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"specifying-a-scheduling-group","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Specifying a scheduling group"},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/workloads/pods/scheduling-group/index.html#specifying-a-scheduling-group","title":null,"children":[]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/command-line-tools-reference/feature-gates/#GenericWorkload","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"GenericWorkload"}]},{"type":"text","value":" feature gate is enabled, you can set the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"spec.schedulingGroup"},{"type":"text","value":" field in your "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Pod"},{"type":"text","value":" manifest. This field establishes a link to a specific "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"PodGroup"},{"type":"text","value":" object in the same namespace by name."}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"yaml","code":"apiVersion: v1\nkind: Pod\nmetadata:\n  name: worker-0\n  namespace: some-ns\nspec:\n  schedulingGroup:\n    podGroupName: training-worker-0\n  containers:\n  - name: ml-worker\n    image: training:v1"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"schedulingGroup"},{"type":"text","value":" field is immutable. Once set, a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Pod"},{"type":"text","value":" cannot be moved to a different "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"PodGroup"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"behavior","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Behavior"},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/workloads/pods/scheduling-group/index.html#behavior","title":null,"children":[]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When you set "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"spec.schedulingGroup"},{"type":"text","value":", the scheduler looks up the referenced "},{"type":"link","href":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/podgroup-api/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"PodGroup"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and applies the "},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/workloads/workload-api/policies/index.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"scheduling policy"}]},{"type":"text","value":" defined in it:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"PodGroup"},{"type":"text","value":" uses the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"basic"},{"type":"text","value":" policy, each "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Pod"},{"type":"text","value":" is scheduled independently using standard Kubernetes behavior. The grouping is used as group-level label."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"PodGroup"},{"type":"text","value":" uses the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"gang"},{"type":"text","value":" policy, the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Pod"},{"type":"text","value":" enters an \"all-or-nothing\" scheduling lifecycle. The scheduler tries to place at least "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"minCount"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Pods"},{"type":"text","value":" in the group simultaneously; none of them bind to nodes unless the minimum is met."}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"missing-podgroup-reference","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Missing PodGroup reference"},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/workloads/pods/scheduling-group/index.html#missing-podgroup-reference","title":null,"children":[]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Pod"},{"type":"text","value":" references a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"PodGroup"},{"type":"text","value":" that does not yet exist, the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Pod"},{"type":"text","value":" remains pending. The scheduler automatically reconsiders the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Pod"},{"type":"text","value":" once the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"PodGroup"},{"type":"text","value":" is created."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This applies regardless of whether the eventual policy is "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"basic"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"gang"},{"type":"text","value":", because the scheduler requires the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"PodGroup"},{"type":"text","value":" to determine the policy."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"what-s-next","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What's next"},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/workloads/pods/scheduling-group/index.html#what-s-next","title":null,"children":[]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Learn about the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/podgroup-api/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"PodGroup API"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and its lifecycle."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read about "},{"type":"link","href":"docs/concepts/workloads/workload-api/policies/index.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"PodGroup scheduling policies"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Understand the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/scheduling-eviction/gang-scheduling/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"gang scheduling"}]},{"type":"text","value":" algorithm."}]}]}]}}
